---
import { ancestryAudit, missingParents } from '../scripts/family/ancestry';
import { sharedById, ADAM, personUrl } from '../data/shared-family';
import { familyMapAncestryById as ancestryPeople, familyMapById, mapProfileUrl, mapEdgeAssessment } from '../data/family-map';
import { candidatePeople, candidateRelationships, candidateById } from '../data/ancestry-candidates';
import { EGBERT } from '../data/ancestry-candidates';
import { legendaryPeople, legendaryChain, legendaryRelationships, chronicleUrl, chronicleCitation } from '../data/legendary-family';
import { relationshipReview } from '../data/ancestry-relationships';
import { ancestryFindings } from '../data/ancestry-research';
import { biblicalPeople, biblicalById, ancientGap } from '../data/biblical-family';
const importedAudit = ancestryAudit();
const audit = ancestryAudit(ADAM, ancestryPeople);
const historicalRoute = audit.paths.find(path=>path.at(-1)===EGBERT)!;
const biblicalRoute = ['bible-noah','bible-lamech','bible-methuselah','bible-enoch','bible-jared','bible-mahalaleel','bible-cainan','bible-enos','bible-seth','bible-adam'];
const traditionRoute = [...historicalRoute, ...legendaryChain.slice(1,-1), ...biblicalRoute];
const gapsByChild = audit.ids.filter(id => missingParents(ancestryPeople[id]).length).sort((a,b) => ancestryPeople[a].name.localeCompare(ancestryPeople[b].name));
---
<section class="ancestry-journey" id="ancestry-journey" aria-labelledby="ancestry-heading" data-ancestry-journey>
  <header><span class="editorial-kicker">The next chapter</span><h2 id="ancestry-heading">How far back can we go?</h2><p>Follow a single trail from Adam (Tom), see where names are missing, and check the records behind the oldest claims. <a href="#adam-eve-route">Follow the proposed path to Adam &amp; Eve ↗</a></p></header>
  <div class="ancestry-stats"><p><strong>{audit.ancestors.length}</strong><span>recorded &amp; candidate ancestors</span></p><p><strong>{audit.longest.length-1}</strong><span>parent links on the longest trail</span></p><p><strong>{audit.gaps.length}</strong><span>unfilled parent positions</span></p></div>
  <p class="shared-provenance">These counts include sourced candidate claims. The longest candidate trail reaches {ancestryPeople[audit.longest.at(-1)!].name} through {audit.longest.length-1} parent links. Its Boyd, Prather, immigrant and Warren connections remain provisional or disputed; each added step links to its evidence review. The imported trail has {importedAudit.longest.length-1} parent links and reaches Henry Degotham (reported 1247), with its own conflicts. Neither trail establishes a connection to biblical Adam and Eve.</p>
  <details class="ancestry-trails" id="adam-eve-route" open>
    <summary>Tom → Adam &amp; Eve · proposed route with a legendary bridge</summary>
    <p><strong>This is a cited research route, not proven descent.</strong> It combines the family’s records, provisional royal candidates, a medieval legendary pedigree, and the biblical narrative. The Boyd date conflict and the Prather, immigrant and Warren bridges remain unresolved. The chronicle includes Woden and claims that Sceaf was Noah’s son; that Sceaf relationship is not in Genesis.</p>
    <p>There are {traditionRoute.length-1} steps in this particular composite route. These are positions in the displayed tradition, not a verified generation count. Every link has its source category below. <a href="/family/?view=all">Open all recorded people on the map ↗</a></p>
    <p class="ancestry-route-jumps">Jump along this route: <a href="#route-mft-35dc6a96-d08a-4625-8252-2e6ab3b6796b">Tom</a> → <a href="#route-candidate-edward-i-england">Edward I</a> → <a href="#route-candidate-egbert">Egbert</a> → <a href="#route-legend-woden">Woden · legend</a> → <a href="#route-bible-noah">Noah</a> → <a href="#route-bible-adam">Adam &amp; Eve</a></p>
    <div class="ancestry-trail-window" tabindex="0" aria-label="Proposed Tom to Adam and Eve route; includes legendary links">
      <ol class="ancestry-trail">{traditionRoute.map((id,i)=>{const p=familyMapById[id];const edge=i>0?mapEdgeAssessment(id,traditionRoute[i-1],'parent'):null;const legend=edge?.sourceKind==='legendary tradition';return <li id={`route-${id}`}><span class="ancestry-generation">{i===0?'You':`#${i}`}</span><div><a href={mapProfileUrl(id)}>{id===ADAM?'Adam Muncie (Tom)':p.name}</a><small>{p.dates} · {p.kind==='legendary'?'legendary tradition':p.kind==='biblical'?'biblical narrative':p.kind==='candidate'?'provisional candidate':'family-provided record'}</small>{i>0 && <a class="ancestry-review-link" href={legend?'#chronicle-legendary-route':edge?.evidenceUrl|| (relationshipReview(id,traditionRoute[i-1])?`#${relationshipReview(id,traditionRoute[i-1])!.finding}`:p.kind==='biblical'?biblicalById[traditionRoute[i-1]].url:mapProfileUrl(traditionRoute[i-1]))}>{legend?'Legendary parent claim · chronicle ↗':p.kind==='biblical'?'Biblical parent claim · Genesis ↗':edge?.evidenceUrl?'Provisional / disputed parent claim · evidence ↗':'Recorded parent claim · profile & review ↗'}</a>}{id==='bible-adam' && <p>Seth’s other named parent: <a href="#bible-eve">Eve ↗</a> · <a href={biblicalById['bible-seth'].url}>Genesis 4:25 ↗</a></p>}</div><a class="ancestry-map-link" href={`/family/?focus=${id}`}>On the map ↗</a></li>})}</ol>
    </div>
    <p><a href="#chronicle-legendary-route">Read the chronicle’s claim and its limits ↗</a></p>
  </details>
  <details class="ancestry-research" id="chronicle-legendary-route">
    <summary>The chronicle bridge · source, conflicts &amp; {legendaryPeople.length} names</summary>
    <p>This preserves one pedigree printed on page 48 of Giles’s Anglo-Saxon Chronicle. From Egbert it runs through Elmund, the early West Saxon names, Woden, and Sceaf to Noah. It supplies evidence that a medieval tradition made these claims; it does not establish those people or relationships as Tom’s ancestors.</p>
    <p>Names and generation counts differ between versions. We retain this page’s sequence rather than combining variants. The identification of Elmund with the king of Kent is disputed. No birth dates, spouses or missing generations have been invented.</p>
    <p><a href={chronicleUrl}>{chronicleCitation} ↗</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://fasg.org/projects/henryproject/data/ealhm000.htm">The Henry Project’s comparison of contradictory early Wessex pedigrees ↗</a></p>
    {legendaryPeople.map(p=>{const claim=legendaryRelationships.find(r=>r.to===p.id)!;return <article id={p.id}><span class="editorial-kicker">Legendary tradition · unverified relationship</span><h3>{p.name}</h3><p>Parent claimed by this chronicle: {familyMapById[claim.from].name}. {claim.note}</p><p>{p.dates}. Unnamed parents remain ? positions on the map.</p><a href={chronicleUrl}>Printed chronicle pedigree, page 48 ↗</a> · <a href={`/family/?focus=${p.id}`}>Explore on the map ↗</a></article>})}
  </details>
  <details class="ancestry-trails" open>
    <summary>Follow one ancestry trail</summary>
    <label class="ancestry-select">Trail endpoint <select data-ancestry-select>{audit.paths.map((path, i) => <option value={i}>{i===0?'Longest · ':''}{ancestryPeople[path.at(-1)!].name} · {path.length-1} parent links{i>0&&audit.paths.slice(0,i).some(p=>p.at(-1)===path.at(-1))?' · another route':''}</option>)}</select></label>
    <p class="ancestry-trail-help">Start at Tom and read downward into earlier generations. Open a name for its full profile, or “On the map” to explore that branch.</p>
    <div class="ancestry-trail-window" tabindex="0" aria-label="Ancestry trail; scroll to earlier generations">
      {audit.paths.map((path, i) => <div data-ancestry-path={i} hidden={i!==0}><ol class="ancestry-trail">{path.map((id, generation) => <li><span class="ancestry-generation">{generation===0?'You':`G${generation}`}</span><div><a href={mapProfileUrl(id)}>{id===ADAM?'Adam Muncie (Tom)':ancestryPeople[id].name}</a><small>{ancestryPeople[id].dates || 'Dates not recorded'} · {candidateById[id]?'provisional candidate':'family-provided'}</small>{generation>0 && mapEdgeAssessment(id,path[generation-1],'parent').evidenceUrl && <a class="ancestry-review-link" href={mapEdgeAssessment(id,path[generation-1],'parent').evidenceUrl}>Provisional parent claim · evidence ↗</a>}{generation>0 && relationshipReview(id,path[generation-1]) && <a class="ancestry-review-link" href={`#${relationshipReview(id,path[generation-1])!.finding}`}>Parent link under review · evidence ↗</a>}</div><a class="ancestry-map-link" href={`/family/?focus=${id}`}>On the map ↗</a></li>)}</ol>
        <div class="ancestry-unknown"><strong>Next generation: parents not recorded</strong><ul>{missingParents(ancestryPeople[path.at(-1)!]).map(g => <li><a href={`#${g.id}`}>? · Unknown parent {g.slot}</a> <span class="family-confidence" data-confidence="provisional">placeholder</span></li>)}</ul><p>Earlier generations remain an open gap. Their number has not been established.</p></div>
      </div>)}
    </div>
    <p role="status" class="ancestry-trail-status" data-ancestry-status>Longest research trail · {audit.longest.length-1} parent links · includes a provisional candidate</p>
  </details>
  <details class="ancestry-gaps"><summary>Explore {audit.gaps.length} missing-parent placeholders</summary><p>Each placeholder has a permanent ID tied to an unfilled immediate parent position. Its identity, sex, dates, and biological or adoptive status are unknown. These are research positions, not additional identified relatives. More distant generations will be added only when their positions can be established.</p><ul class="ancestry-gap-list">{gapsByChild.map(id => <li><a href={mapProfileUrl(id)}>{ancestryPeople[id].name}</a><div>{missingParents(ancestryPeople[id]).map(g => <details id={g.id}><summary>? · Unknown parent {g.slot} <span class="family-confidence" data-confidence={g.confidence}>provisional</span></summary><p>No identity recorded for this position. Source: inference from the imported tree’s incomplete parent entries.</p><small>Stable placeholder: {g.id}</small></details>)}</div></li>)}</ul></details>
  <details class="ancestry-research"><summary>Ancestry research · records, candidates & conflicts</summary><p>Records checked 5–6 October 2026. These findings add evidence and questions alongside the imported account; they do not replace its people or parent links.</p>{ancestryFindings.map(f => <article id={f.id}><h3>{f.title}</h3><span class="family-confidence" data-confidence={f.confidence}>{f.confidence} identity / connection</span> <small>{f.sourceKind}</small><p>{f.finding}</p><p>{f.limit}</p><p><strong>Next record:</strong> {f.next}</p><p class="ancestry-citation"><a href={f.url}>{f.citation} ↗</a></p><p>{f.people.map(id => <a class="ancestry-person-link" href={mapProfileUrl(id)}>{ancestryPeople[id].name} ↗</a>)}</p></article>)}</details>
  <details class="ancestry-research" open><summary>Candidate extensions · {candidatePeople.length} tentative ancestors</summary>{candidatePeople.map(p=>{const claim=candidateRelationships.find(r=>r.from===p.id)!; return <article id={p.id}><h3>{p.name}</h3><span class="family-confidence" data-confidence="provisional">Provisional candidate · compiled claim</span><p>{p.dates}. This is a research identity; dates and parentage are not independently established.</p><p>{claim.note}</p><p><a href={claim.url}>Source pedigree and citations ↗</a> · <a href={`#${claim.finding}`}>Identity, conflicts &amp; parent claim review ↗</a></p><a href={`/family/?focus=${p.id}`}>Explore candidate on the map ↗</a></article>})}</details>
  <div class="ancestry-unresolved"><span class="editorial-kicker">The open gap</span><h3><span class="ancestry-gap-mark" aria-hidden="true">?</span> {ancientGap.label}</h3><p>No established chain joins Tom’s recorded family to a biblical person. The proposed route above crosses this historical gap using an explicitly labelled medieval legend. A source for that tradition is available, but the historical connection remains unestablished.</p></div>
  <details class="ancestry-biblical" open><summary>Explore the biblical genealogy · Adam & Eve to Abram</summary><p>This branch is also searchable in the family map above. It follows the King James text of Genesis 4, 5, and 11. “Textual tradition” means the relationship appears in that text; it is not an independently verified vital record or a proven ancestor of Tom. No calendar birth dates or missing spouses have been invented.</p><div class="ancestry-bible-grid">{biblicalPeople.map(p => <article id={p.id}><span class="editorial-kicker">Biblical narrative · textual tradition</span><h3>{p.name}</h3><a href={`/family/?focus=${p.id}`}>Explore on the family map ↗</a><p>{p.parents.length?`Parents named in this branch: ${p.parents.map(id=>biblicalById[id].name).join(' & ')}`:'No human parent given in the biblical narrative.'}</p><a href={p.url}>{p.verse} · KJV ↗</a><small>Stable ID: {p.id}</small></article>)}</div></details>
  <noscript><p>Every trail remains available without scripting through the person profiles: follow their parent entries. The missing-parent and biblical sections above also work without scripting.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>
  function initAncestry() {
    const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-ancestry-journey]');
    if (!root || root.dataset.initialized) return;
    root.dataset.initialized = 'true';
    const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-ancestry-select]')!;
    select.addEventListener('change', () => {
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ancestry-path]').forEach(path => path.hidden = path.dataset.ancestryPath !== select.value);
      root.querySelector('.ancestry-trail-window')?.scrollTo({top:0});
      root.querySelector('[data-ancestry-status]')!.textContent = `${select.selectedOptions[0].textContent} · recorded / candidate assertions`;
    });
    const revealGap = () => {
      const target = document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));
      if (!target || target === root || !root.contains(target)) return;
      let parent: HTMLElement | null = target;
      while (parent && parent !== root) { if (parent instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) parent.open = true; parent = parent.parentElement; }
      target.scrollIntoView({block:'center'});
    };
    root.addEventListener('click', event => {
      const target = event.target instanceof Element ? event.target.closest<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[href^="#gap-"]') : null;
      if (target) { const gap = document.getElementById(target.hash.slice(1)); if (gap) { root.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('.ancestry-gaps')!.open = true; (gap as HTMLDetailsElement).open = true; } }
    });
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', revealGap);
    revealGap();
    document.addEventListener('astro:before-swap', () => window.removeEventListener('hashchange', revealGap), {once:true});
  }
  initAncestry(); document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initAncestry);
</script>
